      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's hitting the right tone. i think the speech needs a final closing statement that really brings it home. can you write a concluding paragraph that basically says that if you don't show up, you don't have the right to complain about how things turn out? like, you can't claim to care about your community but then refuse to actually participate in it. make it sound like participation is the tax you pay for having a voice.",
